<title>DUBAI: United Saudi Commercial Bank Q1 net profit up.</title>
<headline>United Saudi Commercial Bank Q1 net profit up.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			 (million riyals unless stated)</p>
<p> Net profit		     91.39	vs	 84.46</p>
<p> Total operating income    219.62	vs	204.58</p>
<p> Total operating expenses  135.77	vs	130.96</p>
<p> Net operating profit	 83.84	vs	 73.61</p>
<p> Net fixed assets	     51.20	vs	 32.94</p>
<p> Investment securities   3,463.38	vs    1,820.95</p>
<p>Full Name: United Saudi Commercial Bank</p>
<p>Note: Bank Melli Iran owns 10 percent of the Riyadh-based bank.</p>
<p>The bank said income from investment securities registered a substantial growth due to the deployment of excess liquidity in the bank's investment portfolio. -- Dubai newsroom +9714 6071 219</p>
</text>
